# wave-sets-timing.vrs: wave-sets D23 (Session 1, first boot): ws-three with its waves left alive holds 10 or more
# tracked units for eleven timing windows, for -TimingSpan -Windows 10 -MinTracked 10. At the pond: the ravine is
# close enough to the castle that a wave's centre can land in its territory (wave 1 skipped there).
# ws-three runs 1800 s here with every entry CHAR_Undead_SkeletonSoldier_Armored_Farbane at level 30: the Withered
# skeletons of the other runs decay or fall to native units within about ten minutes (a wave cleared with no kill),
# and the span needs a health line of 10+ tracked, eleven one-minute windows and the next health line 10 minutes on.
# Needs: what wave-sets.vrs needs; Chaos invulnerable (kept invulnerable: `ToggleInvulnerable true`, never false).
ensure
console TPHome
wait 3
chat .devgo pond
expect-log \[DEV TP\] pond
wait 4
chat .nyar event reload
expect-log events: reloaded
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
mark
chat .nyar event start ws-three
expect-log event ws-three wave 1/3 timeout=30
expect-log wave 2(/3| of ws-three skipped) timeout=140
wait 1500
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units:
chat .nyar event stop ws-three
expect-log event ws-three stopped
wait 40
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0
